# Database rules

- Every schema change must be delivered through Flyway migration.
- Do not edit older migrations that may already be applied in shared environments.
- Prefer additive, backward-compatible migrations when possible.
- Be explicit about indexes, nullability, defaults, and foreign keys.
- Keep entity mappings simple and readable.
- Avoid eager fetching unless strongly justified.
- Call out transactional implications and data migration risks when changing persistence behavior.
